A||||18||fldevel||Racing a beemer ... need quick horsepower ||||1||
Z||000000||fldevel||08-21-2000||01:07 PM||||im racing a BMW on a little road coarse we made up ...i know i can get him in the corners but im worried about acceleration and horse power .. any little tips on quick mods and preps to get the extra punch ?? <P> thanks all ..oh ya .. i have an 85,GT v-6 ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-21-2000||01:11 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nosnitrous.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.electricsupercharger.com" TARGET=_blank>www.electricsupercharger.com</A> <P>throtle body coolant bypass, K&N (not a big dif but every bit helps.. # e-0890)take the passenger seat out, take the spare tire and it's accessories out less weight!  that about it for the easy stuff... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||whamel||08-21-2000||01:32 PM||||Which model BMW?  That's a good start to tell how far you have to stretch or if you're close.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||08-21-2000||01:57 PM||||i believe its a newer model Z-3 r sumthing like that "tells you how much i know about BMW's "  and car must be stock with no fuel system mods ... am i screwed ?? well.. i took the tire jack out if that helps any ?? lol .. nothing was sed about intake except for no superchargers or forced induction and nothing was sed about exhaust ..this is pretty much a stock race around some tight cornered backroads to give you an idea <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fldevel (edited 08-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||08-21-2000||02:03 PM||||if its a z3 with the straight 6 your toast but if its the I4 one you might stand a chance, I couldnt even hang with the straight 6 Z3 in my formula and it has the good suspension with all new parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> acceleration wise the I4 Z3 should be close to your GTs acceleration, but if it has dual exhaust, dont even bother... <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formula_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||08-21-2000||02:26 PM||||I got to drive a friend's 1996 BMW Z3 (4 cyl automatic) about a month ago.  It was disappointingly slow with an exhaust note like a single-cam Saturn.  It has no punch whatsoever below 3000 rpm.<P>If your friend's BMW is a 6, you're in for a race, but if he has a 4-cyl, I think you'll beat him easily even if he has a 5-speed.  Have fun!||||reg||13
Z||000006||whamel||08-21-2000||02:32 PM||||As a card carrying member of the BMW club, I can tell you that if it's a straight 6 then you're hosed all around.  I doubt you could out handle it either.  If it's a '96 you should have little trouble beating it, but other years shouldn't be too out of line.  If it's stock (and a 2000) you're looking at about:<BR>for the 2.5 170HP @ 5500 RPM & 181 @ 3500 RPM<BR>and for the 2.8 193 @ 5500 RPM & 206 @ 3500 RPM<BR>    My friend has a '96 with the 1.9 and it's pretty easy to beat, but in '99 even the small 4 got competitive.  There are some pretty good suspension techniques for these that really can improve handling so if it's been tuned and modded you may be in a bit over your head.  Never hurts to try though, right? <BR>Wade<BR>P.S. Keep in mind the weight difference between the 4 cylinder Z and the GT is only slightly over 100 pounds or so.  <p>[This message has been edited by whamel (edited 08-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||HugGRRRFiero||08-21-2000||02:38 PM||||Bolt on one of these side scoops and get a few more HP at speed!  Every little bit counts...<P><A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bbjproducts/" TARGET=_blank>BBJ Side Scoops</A><P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000008||ezsurf||08-21-2000||02:49 PM||||Remove your air filter for the race, even if it's a K&N.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fldevel||08-22-2000||12:21 PM|||| i got him guys ... it was a 6-cyl z-3 he had me on the start but after the first turn it was all handleing from there .. speeds never really got over 80 mph ..hit the first turn at about 60 and passed him on the inside as he slid to the outside of the corner ..then i lost sight of him as i was doing between 65-70 mph through the S curves  ..crossed the finish line and waited about 3 min later here he comes ..lol ..this was mostly for fun .. neither of us had anything to gain or loose ..although i had fun whiping through the backroads legaly ..thanks guys for all the tips ..was one hell of a rush ||||reg||1
